<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Géza, Grand Prince of the Hungarians</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 940–997</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Géza of Hungary</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Géza was Grand Prince of the Hungarians from about 972 until his death in 997, a member of the Árpád dynasty. He made peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, invited Western missionaries and was baptised, beginning the conversion of the Hungarians to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. He married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarolt">Sarolt</a>, daughter of the gyula of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>, and prepared the succession of their son Stephen, crowned the first King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> in 1000 or 1001.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/geza-grand-prince-of-the-hungarians.jpg" alt="Géza, Grand Prince of the Hungarians" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Márk Kálti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Geza-ChroniconPictum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
